# SpecKit Constitution — Go POS SaaS POS Backend

## Article I — Correctness
The database is the source of truth. Business invariants must be transactionally enforced.

## Article II — Multi-tenancy
Tenant isolation is mandatory at both application authorization and PostgreSQL RLS layers.

## Article III — Security
Secrets are externalized. Authentication and authorization are separate concerns. Access tokens are short-lived and refresh tokens rotate with replay detection.

## Article IV — Data integrity
Money uses exact arithmetic. Idempotency protects retryable writes. Database constraints enforce uniqueness and referential integrity.

## Article V — Maintainability
Handlers are thin, use cases own business behavior, repositories own SQL, and all I/O is context-aware.

## Article VI — Compatibility
The Flutter client API contract is versioned and changes must be backward-compatible or explicitly versioned.

## Article VII — Observability
Every request has correlation/request identity. Errors and latency are measurable without leaking secrets.

## Article VIII — Quality
Code is not complete without tests, static checks, security checks, documentation, and operational consideration.
